From: 1358 <1583407+1358@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:46:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [ActiveAE] Keep the sink delay when an IEC packet is dropped

SyncStream drops a late passthrough packet by setting nb_samples to 0,
for packed IEC streams as well. The packer then emits no frames, so the
delay query is skipped and the engine is told the sink is empty. The
following sync errors are off by the sink delay, and the player moves
its clock after every such correction.

(cherry picked from commit 9a83eedf8b151f8388f088619e8d6c1301ffef33)
---
 xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESink.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESink.cpp b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESink.cpp
index 4ab83e9..95d8b13 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESink.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Engines/ActiveAE/ActiveAESink.cpp
@@ -1716,7 +1716,7 @@ unsigned int CActiveAESink::OutputSamples(CSampleBuffer* samples)
     // A packet dropped for a/v sync has no frames and never enters the loop above. Query the
     // sink anyway, otherwise the engine is told the sink holds no audio at all and the next
     // sync error measurements are off by the whole sink delay.
-    if (!m_needIecPack && totalFrames == 0)
+    if (totalFrames == 0)
       m_sink->GetDelay(status);
     // (Hades: a packet left out for the sync was not counted by the engine, CActiveAE::RunStages())
     const bool counted{samples->pool &&
